    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To argue that current \"meritocratic\" and \"property rights\" systems perpetuate the racial wealth gap, you must demonstrate that they rely on **unfair advantages in the \"merit\" calculus** rather than actual superior effort. You can frame \"meritocracy\" as a myth because the starting line is unjust for marginalized groups, and \"private property\" historically protected the very exclusion of non-wealthy (and often non-white) people from building generational equity.\n\nBy highlighting that the system is **fundamentally broken** when it demands equal *opportunity from a deeply unequal starting position* while using \"neutral\" laws as a shield against \"unfair\" historical advantages, you can show that true equality is impossible without correcting these deep structural imbalances. This approach moves beyond simple \"unfairness\" to show that the current economic model is self-defeating for social progress.",
